WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.400
Pulling up to another day of Tesla's short-time daily, episode 488 coming to you from Vancouver,

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:14.660
it's May 27th, 2026. Tesla never sleeps and neither does the news cycle. Tesla's scrapped India factory

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:21.280
hands local EV rivals an open runway in a market at once targeted for growth. Tesla has abandoned

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:27.840
long-disgusted plans for a factory in India after repeated delays. Rivals have already begun setting

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:33.340
up local production and sales operations in the country. The move leaves Tesla without a manufacturing

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:38.660
foothold in one of the fastest-growing auto markets. The decision follows years of negotiations

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:44.540
that never produced a firm timeline or site. Observers will watch whether Tesla shifts to imports

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:50.500
or reopens talks with state governments. While Tesla steps back from one major market expansion,

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:55.160
its financial ties to another high-growth company continue to quietly strengthen.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:01:02.380
Tesla maintains an ownership position in SpaceX along with nearly $890 million in associated

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:09.920
revenue. An eventual SpaceX IPO could unlock additional value for Tesla shareholders. The relationship

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:15.720
also includes shared technology and supplier arrangements between the two companies. Investors

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:20.600
are tracking how any public listing might affect Tesla's balance sheet and valuation multiples.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:27.500
That cross-company relationship is also playing out in NASA contracts. NASA plans to add six

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:33.660
additional post-certification missions to SpaceX's existing commercial crew contract. Up to three

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:37.940
missions could be ordered immediately, with the rest available through the end of the International

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:44.880
Space Station program. Boeing's ongoing certification delays created the opening for the expanded order.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:51.040
The decision reinforces SpaceX's role as the primary US crew transport provider for the

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:56.980
foreseeable future. The same energy storage technology that supports SpaceX operations is now

00:01:56.980 --> 00:02:02.720
scaling in other markets. A new megapack to Excel deployment in New Zealand is now supplying

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:10.320
power to approximately 44,000 homes. This marks the first installation of the larger 2xL variant in

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:17.000
that market. The project adds grid-scale storage capacity in a region expanding renewable integration.

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:23.440
Meta and Enbridge have contracted Tesla for roughly $200 million worth of battery storage

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:29.260
tied to a large clean energy data center. The installation will support power reliability

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:36.160
and renewable integration at the site. Tesla's megapack systems were selected for the scale and speed

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:42.480
of deployment required. On the vehicle side, Tesla is preparing infrastructure for its next autonomy

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:49.660
push. Tesla is preparing a purpose-built facility in Texas to support future robotaxi operations.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:56.560
The hub is expected to handle vehicle charging, cleaning, and dispatch coordination. Site selection

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:02.260
and permitting work are already underway according to local reports. The project aligns with broader

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:08.740
plans to scale unsupervised autonomy services in the state. While autonomy infrastructure advances,

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:14.820
development priorities on existing models remain selective. Tesla holds the components needed for

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:20.640
a higher performance model three variant but has chosen not to assemble them. The company has

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:26.160
instead focused development resources on other programs. This leaves the current model three

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:31.900
performance as the top trim in that lineup for now. Production capacity and software priorities

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:37.580
appear to have taken precedence over adding another plaid model. Engineering teams have confirmed

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:42.540
the necessary motors, inverters, and cooling components already exist in inventory.

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:48.920
broader vehicle programs are also moving forward at different speeds. Development work on

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:54.180
Tesla's next mass market vehicle continues to advance through prototype and tooling stages.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:59.460
The program remains focused on cost reduction and simplified manufacturing processes.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:05.740
No firm production timeline has been released, though internal milestones are reportedly being met.

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:12.360
Suppliers are receiving updated specifications as the design stabilizes. Taking a step back from

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:19.140
today's headlines, the quiet accumulation of nearly $890 million in SpaceX-related revenue

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:24.540
challenges the assumption that Tesla's valuation rests solely on its automotive and energy

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:29.980
businesses. The ownership state creates a direct financial bridge between two companies that

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:35.200
already share engineering talent and component supply chains. Data from regulatory

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:40.100
filings show this revenue stream has grown steadily without requiring additional Tesla

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:46.240
capital expenditure. The mechanism is straightforward because Tesla's early investment in SpaceX now

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:51.420
generates recurring income while the underlying equity position sits on the balance sheet at a

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:57.840
fraction of current private market valuations. When SpaceX eventually lists publicly, Tesla could

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:03.240
realize a one-time gain or ongoing dividend flow depending on how the shares are handled.

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:09.240
Any future monetization of the SpaceX position would provide non-delutive capital that could

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:15.600
accelerate robotaxi or optimist programs without new equity raises. Keep an eye on supplier updates

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:21.960
tied to the next mass market vehicle, as internal milestones continue. That's your Tesla news for

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:33.920
today. TSLA closed at $440.36, up $6.77, 1.6%. If you found this useful, a rating or review on

